opentune-mapfind
================

This crate proposes candidate calibration maps from a single ECU image.

The general approach -- scan for monotonic breakpoint axes, pair adjacent axes
and promote the following block to a candidate table, score it by axis
plausibility and surface smoothness, and attach only probabilistic,
evidence-based labels instead of claimed map names -- was learned from the
described behaviour of:

    openremap-core -- https://github.com/v-arapidis/openremap-core
      (openremap/core/services/maps/map_hunter.py, map_classifier.py)
      Copyright (c) V. Arapidis, licensed MIT.

This crate is an independent re-implementation in Rust: its own types, its own
count-header layouts ([n1][n2][axis1][axis2][data] and [n][axis][data], 8- and
16-bit, big- and little-endian), its own scoring formula and classifier rules,
and no source text taken from openremap-core. The MIT licence is compatible with
OpenTune's GPL-3.0-or-later; this notice is the attribution it asks for.

No ECU images are shipped with this crate.
